<p>An Iranian warship that Sri Lankan officials identified as the IRIS Dena sank off Sri Lanka’s southern coast on March 4 after sending a distress call, triggering a search-and-rescue effort by Sri Lanka’s navy and air force. Sri Lanka said it rescued 32 people and recovered several bodies from the sea; officials put the number on board at about 180. U.S. officials told Reuters the United States carried out the strike that hit the ship, and U.S. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth publicly confirmed that a U.S. submarine sank it. Sri Lankan sources cited by Reuters described a “suspected submarine attack,” but early accounts differed on how many were missing or wounded, and Sri Lanka’s navy spokesman rejected claims that 101 people were missing.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/SFU8ju1oD0QRv93drpgR1PGVe3C0XVFUv8uw4rfD2EsIVN1CLr0Fai0C7l6EOCO4jo4OPZI-4u50qQJ2JxQMGfmpTPkOTDQ8KXgW87tztC9FJAyCRTspT2fqm3ewQyXRn1nV4OvJ2J1lPTP5ROAHIaQfgppzziDsVpDM3etIHjfAYvIX1WDglB1esMTfXEoQsYB3TNrW_eLmXPUGsSzaOkOFtulHaw' alt='An ambulance at the naval headquarters in Galle, Sri Lanka, on Wednesday after the sinking.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Medical response: Sri Lankan officials said the rescued sailors were taken to Karapitiya Hospital in Galle for treatment.</li><li>Ship identification and type: Sri Lankan officials identified the vessel as the IRIS Dena; Reuters-linked reporting described it as a Moudge-class frigate in Iran’s Southern Fleet.</li><li>Casualty-figure uncertainty: Reuters sources in Sri Lanka’s navy and defence ministry said at least 101 were missing, 78 were wounded and one person had died, but a Sri Lankan navy spokesman said the “101 missing” report was untrue.</li><li>U.S. confirmation and framing: Hegseth said a U.S. submarine sank the ship, which The Guardian described as the first U.S. attack on Iranian forces outside the Middle East during the conflict.</li><li>Pre-incident activity: A ship named “IRINS Dena” was listed as taking part in a Bay of Bengal naval drill from Feb. 18 to 25, according to the exercise website cited by SCMP.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Defense Department: U.S. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said a U.S. submarine sank the Iranian warship off Sri Lanka’s coast. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/04/us-submarine-torpedo-iran-warship-sri-lanka-coast-pete-hegseth'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Sri Lanka Foreign Ministry: Foreign Minister Vijitha Herath said Sri Lanka responded out of treaty-based humanitarian obligations to help vessels in distress, regardless of nationality. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/633720-sri-lankan-navy-rescues-30/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Sri Lanka Navy spokesman: Navy spokesman Buddhika Sampath said rescuers recovered several bodies, and he also pushed back on reports that 101 people were missing. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/633720-sri-lankan-navy-rescues-30/'>RT</a>)</li><li>U.S. officials (anonymous): Three U.S. officials told Reuters the United States carried out the strike, and one said a U.S. submarine conducted it. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/exclusive-us-carried-out-strike-iranian-warship-sri-lanka-coast-officials-say'>Al-Monitor (Reuters)</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera reporting: Al Jazeera said the cause of the sinking was still unclear, reflecting uncertainty in early reporting even as the rescue continued. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/4/at-least-100-missing-after-iranian-military-ship-sinks-off-sri-lanka-coast'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/south-asia/article/3345425/sri-lanka-rescues-32-critically-wounded-sailors-sunk-iranian-warship'>Hegseth says US submarine sank Iranian warship off Sri Lanka</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/633720-sri-lankan-navy-rescues-30/'>Submarine sinks Iranian warship off coast of Sri Lanka – Reuters</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/strike-on-iranian-warship-off-sri-lanka-us-israel-iran-war/article70703655.ece'>U.S. carried out strike on Iranian warship off Sri Lanka coast, Pentagon chief says</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/over-100-missing-dozens-wounded-after-submarine-attack-on-iranian-ship-near-sri-lanka-amid-us-israel-iran-war-west-asia-crisis-13986137.html'>Over 100 missing, dozens wounded after submarine attack on Iranian ship near Sri Lanka</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/04/world/middleeast/iran-navy-ship-sri-lanka.html'>Iranian Navy Ship Sinks Near Coast of Sri Lanka, With Dozens Feared Dead</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/exclusive-us-carried-out-strike-iranian-warship-sri-lanka-coast-officials-say'>Exclusive-US carried out strike on Iranian warship off Sri Lanka coast, officials say</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/4/at-least-100-missing-after-iranian-military-ship-sinks-off-sri-lanka-coast'>At least 100 people missing after Iranian military ship sinks off Sri Lanka</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/mar/04/iran-war-live-updates-us-israel-latest-news-strait-of-hormuz-middle-east-crisis'>Middle East crisis live: US submarine sank Iranian warship, Hegseth confirms; Israel launches ‘wave of strikes’ on Tehran</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-confirms-its-submarine-sank-iranian-warship-off-sri-lanka-coast-11168177#publisher=newsstand'>US Confirms Its Submarine Sank Iranian Warship Off Sri Lanka Coast</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/sri-lanka-rescues-30-people-on-board-distressed-iranian-ship-foreign-minister-says'>Hegseth says U.S. sub sank Iranian warship off Sri Lanka</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/least-101-people-missing-after-submarine-attack-iranian-s